Spring Boot:-Spring Boot is a Java Framework that makes it esier to
create and run Java Apllication.

It simplifies the the configuration and setup process,allowing
developers to focus more on writing code for their application.

->Spring Boot is a Module of Spring FrameWork.

->It facilitates Rapid Application Development.

->Spring Boot is an open source Java Framework used to create a 
web appln.

->it is developed by  Pivotal Team.

->It is a combination of Spring Framework and Embeded servers.

->The main goal of Spring Boot is is to reduce development,unit test,
and integration test time and in Spring Boot there is no requirement
for XML configuration.


**Spring Boot follows a layered architecture:-
->It consists of 4 layers:-
1.Presentation layer:-It handles HTTP requests,authentication
and JSON conversion.

2.Business layer:-Contains Business logic,validation and
authorization.


3.Persistence Layer:-Manages database interactions using ORM 
frameworks like Spring Data JPA.

4.Database Layer:-Stores application data using relational
database and NoSql database.
